{"explanation":"The matrix sends each point \((x,y)\) to \((2x+y,y)\): it stretches horizontally and shears the plane while leaving vertical coordinates unchanged. The unit square becomes a parallelogram spanned by \((2,0)\) and \((1,1)\). Its area is 2, matching the determinant \(2\); use the slider to watch the area factor grow from 1 to 2.","manimCode":"const title = new Text({ text: 'Stretch + shear', color: WHITE, fontSize: 34 });
